<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="PentUpHouse-G-Theme" spTempo="190">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1956
Composer:	Sonny Rollins
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	16-bar AABA
Style:	Hard bop swing
Key:	G major

“Pent-Up House” was composed by Sonny Rollins
and first recorded in 1956 for Sonny Rollins Plus 4,
featuring Clifford Brown, Max Roach, Richie Powell,
and George Morrow. Its compact AABA design uses
recurring ii–V progressions and rhythmically driving
phrases, making it a prominent example of Rollins’s
hard-bop writing.</spComments>
